        "original_id": "dcc31f58-3f55-55be-a855-87cdf1e1e97b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ross Pople, Michael Tippett, Yehudi Menuhin, Clifford Curzon, David Oistrakh, Louis Kentner, George Malcolm, Adrian Boult, Rudolf Kempe, Benjamin Britten, Witold Lutosławski, Krzysztof Penderecki, Georg Solti, Leonard Bernstein, George Benjamin, John Casken, Edwin Roxburgh, Luciano Berio, John Tavener, Malcolm Arnold, Pierre Boulez\n- Roles: conductors, composers, soloists\n- Organizations: orchestras, choirs\n- Works: A Child of Our Time, Fantasia Concertante on a Theme of Corelli, The Midsummer Marriage\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Tippett was born on 2 January 1905 and died on 8 January 1998.\n- Michael Tippett was an English composer who rose to prominence during and immediately after the Second World War.\n- Michael Tippett's best-known works include the oratorio \"A Child of Our Time,\" the orchestral work \"Fantasia Concertante on a Theme of Corelli,\" and the opera \"The Midsummer Marriage.\"\n- Ross Pople has worked with Yehudi Menuhin, Clifford Curzon, David Oistrakh, Louis Kentner, George Malcolm, Sir Adrian Boult, Rudolf Kempe, Benjamin Britten, Witold Lutosławski, Krzysztof Penderecki, Michael Tippett, Georg Solti, Leonard Bernstein, George Benjamin, John Casken, Edwin Roxburgh, Luciano Berio, John Tavener, Malcolm Arnold, and Pierre Boulez.\n- Ross Pople has also worked with many major orchestras, choirs, and soloists.",
